   "quote": "egress restricted exclusively to the PostgreSQL database security group"
  }
 ],
 "notes": "AZ names are inference space: db subnets must span two AZs (distinct_path) and the lambda and bastion subnets must share the AZ of lambda-rds-db-subnet-1 (join), which is what 'primary zone' means. Port checks require TCP so an all-protocol rule does not satisfy them. Bastion egress to the DB group via a separate rule must be CIDR-less (source-group) so the DB group's own egress rule cannot satisfy it. Known Partial: 'egress strictly to 10.32.0.0/20' is enforced as every-CIDR for inline egress blocks; with separate rule resources an added 0.0.0.0/0 rule cannot be ruled out, because a rule-to-group link is a reference and the schema cannot negate a reference."
}
